      <h3 id="ipi-verifying-nodes-after-installation_ocp-installation-overview" class="group scroll-mt-20">Verifying node state after installation<a href="#ipi-verifying-nodes-after-installation_ocp-installation-overview" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h3>
      <p class="_abstract">The OpenShift Container Platform installation completes when the following installation health checks are successful:</p>
      <ul>
      <li>The provisioner can access the OpenShift Container Platform web console.</li>
      <li>All control plane nodes are ready.</li>
      <li>All cluster Operators are available.</li>
      </ul>
      <Alert variant="note" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Note</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>After the installation completes, the specific cluster Operators responsible for the worker nodes continuously attempt to provision all worker nodes. Some time is required before all worker nodes report as <code>READY</code>. For installations on bare metal, wait a minimum of 60 minutes before troubleshooting a worker node. For installations on all other platforms, wait a minimum of 40 minutes before troubleshooting a worker node. A <code>DEGRADED</code> state for the cluster Operators responsible for the worker nodes depends on the Operators' own resources and not on the state of the nodes.</p>
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      <p>After your installation completes, you can continue to monitor the condition of the nodes in your cluster.</p>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul><li>The installation program resolves successfully in the terminal.</li></ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Show the status of all worker nodes:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get nodes"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"NAME                           STATUS   ROLES    AGE   VERSION\nexample-compute1.example.com   Ready    worker   13m   v1.21.6+bb8d50a\nexample-compute2.example.com   Ready    worker   13m   v1.21.6+bb8d50a\nexample-compute4.example.com   Ready    worker   14m   v1.21.6+bb8d50a\nexample-control1.example.com   Ready    master   52m   v1.21.6+bb8d50a\nexample-control2.example.com   Ready    master   55m   v1.21.6+bb8d50a\nexample-control3.example.com   Ready    master   55m   v1.21.6+bb8d50a"} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Show the phase of all worker machine nodes:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get machines -A"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"NAMESPACE               NAME                           PHASE         TYPE   REGION   ZONE   AGE\nopenshift-machine-api   example-zbbt6-master-0         Running                              95m\nopenshift-machine-api   example-zbbt6-master-1         Running                              95m\nopenshift-machine-api   example-zbbt6-master-2         Running                              95m\nopenshift-machine-api   example-zbbt6-worker-0-25bhp   Running                              49m\nopenshift-machine-api   example-zbbt6-worker-0-8b4c2   Running                              49m\nopenshift-machine-api   example-zbbt6-worker-0-jkbqt   Running                              49m\nopenshift-machine-api   example-zbbt6-worker-0-qrl5b   Running                              49m"} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      </ol>
